    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": {
        "en": "Reading a job advert"
      },
      "texto": {
        "en": "Many job adverts use **se** to leave the employer unnamed: **se busca una persona**; **se buscan dos personas**. In this pattern, the verb agrees with the noun that follows. You may also see **se requiere** experiencia, **se ofrece** un contrato or **se valorará** el inglés.\n\nA vacancy may require **experiencia**, **formación**, **idiomas**, **disponibilidad** or a **carné de conducir**. It may offer a **contrato**, a **sueldo**, a flexible **horario**, training paid for by the company or the possibility of **ascenso**. Conditions vary from one job to another.\n\nThe application steps are to **enviar el currículum** and a covering letter, **acudir a una entrevista** and, if selected, **firmar el contrato**. Later, someone may **despedirte**; you may **dimitir** or **jubilarte**.\n\nA worker may be **empleado/a**, **estudiante en prácticas**, **autónomo/a** or **funcionario/a**. In an office, you can prepare an **informe**, a **presupuesto** or a **presentación**, and work in **el departamento de ventas**, **el de contabilidad** or **el de recursos humanos**."
      }
    },
